content:
`dispatch` has three parameters, not two:

```ts
dispatch(
  actionOrActions: TAction | TAction[] | undefined,
  onErrors?: (errors: Error[]) => void,
  onSuccess?: (result: PHDocument) => void,
): void
```

`onErrors` surfaces per-action reducer failures; `onSuccess` hands you the updated document the moment the operation lands, which is what you want when the next UI step depends on server-assigned data (a new revision number, a header field) rather than on the action input you already have.

The implementation is `dispatchActions` in `packages/reactor-browser/src/actions/dispatch.ts`, and the ordering there matters. It resolves the document, signs the actions, queues them, and only then runs the callbacks:

```ts
const result = await queueActions(document, signedActionsWithContext);

if (onErrors && result) {
  const errors = getActionErrors(result, signedActionsWithContext);
  if (errors.length) onErrors(errors);
}
if (onSuccess && result) onSuccess(result);
```

Both callbacks are guarded on `result`, so **neither fires** when the dispatch bailed out early — an unresolvable document id or a failure to build signed actions logs an error and returns `undefined` without notifying either callback. `onSuccess` is also not exclusive of `onErrors`: `result` is the document after the operations were appended, and a reducer that threw still produces an operation carrying `.error`. So a dispatch whose actions all failed validation can invoke `onErrors` **and then** `onSuccess` with the (state-unchanged) document. Treat `onSuccess` as "the write round-tripped", not as "the write was accepted".

Documentation caveat: `04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md` still prints the two-argument signature everywhere, including in the "Dispatch Function" key-concepts section and in every hook's return type. The three-argument form is documented only in the learn-path page and is confirmed by source.

_Source: packages/reactor-browser/src/actions/dispatch.ts and src/hooks/dispatch.ts, plus apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/04-editors/03-editor-hooks-and-state.mdx (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._
